><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250509101804+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250509101808+10'00'" name="12814b36-97e4-421b-abca-0fef3f775b92" page="5" coords="313.001000,282.607000,575.969000,282.607000,313.001000,271.577000,575.969000,271.577000,313.001000,271.608000,576.009000,271.608000,313.001000,260.579000,576.009000,260.579000,313.001000,260.610000,575.974000,260.610000,313.001000,249.580000,575.974000,249.580000,313.001000,249.612000,576.009000,249.612000,313.001000,238.582000,576.009000,238.582000,313.001000,238.614000,575.951000,238.614000,313.001000,227.584000,575.951000,227.584000,313.003000,227.616000,576.001000,227.616000,313.003000,216.586000,576.001000,216.586000,313.003000,216.618000,575.997000,216.618000,313.003000,205.588000,575.997000,205.588000,313.003000,205.620000,575.968000,205.620000,313.003000,194.590000,575.968000,194.590000,313.003000,194.622000,419.216000,194.622000,313.003000,183.592000,419.216000,183.592000" rect="312.657000,183.247000,576.354000,282.951000" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Very high CHO diets (10–12 g/kg/day), such as those practiced by&#xD;endurance athletes as part of gut-training strategies, do not have a&#xD;clear impact on iron regulation in elite athletes. Our data confirms&#xD;previous research demonstrating that serum ferritin levels have a&#xD;strong influence on postexercise hepcidin concentrations (</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>McKay&#xD;et al., 2019b</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>; </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Peeling et al., 2014</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>; </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Peeling et al., 2017</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>). Moreover,&#xD;ambient temperature may also be associated with the increase in&#xD;hepcidin concentrations 3 hr postexercise; this relationship warrants&#xD;further investigation.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="612.217000,21.601700,796.144000,282.765000"
/></highlight
